  "tagline": "Sorted, distributed key-value store on HDFS with cell-level security labels.",
  "description": "Accumulo began at the NSA in 2008 as a Bigtable implementation and was donated to Apache in 2011. Like HBase it stores sorted key-value pairs in tablets over HDFS with ZooKeeper coordination, but it adds two distinctive features: visibility labels on every cell, so one table can serve users with different clearances, and server-side iterators that filter or aggregate data during scans and compactions. It remains relevant in government, defence and other security-sensitive environments; elsewhere it is a niche choice with a small community.",
